<dialog class="project-modal" id="modal-zum" aria-labelledby="modal-zum-title">
  <div class="project-modal-inner">
    <button type="button" class="modal-close" data-modal-close aria-label="Close dialog">&times;</button>
    <span class="badge">Web App</span>
    <h3 class="modal-title" id="modal-zum-title">ZUM Quiz — Interactive Web Application</h3>

    <h4 class="modal-heading">Features</h4>
    <p class="modal-text">Quiz configuration — choose category, difficulty and number of questions — plus a timer, progress tracking, a results summary and quiz history.</p>

    <h4 class="modal-heading">API</h4>
    <p class="modal-text">Questions are pulled live from the Open Trivia Database API based on the selected configuration.</p>

    <h4 class="modal-heading">State Management</h4>
    <p class="modal-text">Built with React, managing quiz state — current question, score, timer, and progress — across the session.</p>

    <h4 class="modal-heading">Timer</h4>
    <p class="modal-text">A countdown timer keeps each question timed, adding pacing to the quiz flow.</p>

    <h4 class="modal-heading">Results</h4>
    <p class="modal-text">At the end of a quiz, results are summarized — score and how it compares with previous attempts.</p>

    <h4 class="modal-heading">LocalStorage</h4>
    <p class="modal-text">Quiz history and settings persist locally in the browser via LocalStorage, so past results are still there on return visits.</p>

    <div class="modal-tech-badges">
      <span class="badge">React</span>
      <span class="badge">Tailwind CSS</span>
      <span class="badge">Vite</span>
      <span class="badge">Open Trivia DB API</span>
      <span class="badge">LocalStorage</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</dialog>
